The reference documents in skills/x-algo-kb/references/ quote short excerpts of
upstream source code and reproduce production parameter default values, each
attributed with a `path:line` citation relative to the upstream repository root
at the commit above. Those excerpts remain under the upstream Apache License 2.0.

No upstream source tree is vendored into this repository. scripts/fetch-source.sh
retrieves the pinned commit from upstream on demand.

Upstream deliberately withholds some material (Grox LLM prompt templates, some
botmaker rules, several policy YAML files, and certain numeric operating points
which are replaced with sentinel or mock values). This knowledge base marks those
gaps explicitly rather than inferring them. Where a document says a value is
"not public", no claim about the production value is being made.

